  "doc.title": "How LLVM Compiles Your Code · A Hands-on Essay",
  "doc.desc": "What actually happens inside clang -O2 sum.c between C syntax and AArch64 or x86_64 instructions? Verified directly against host Apple Clang 21.0.0 (LLVM 21), this essay traces the entire chain: the N+1+M decoupled pipeline, -O0 stack allocas, SSA phi insertion via dominance frontiers, fixed-point pass iteration, loop hoisting and SIMD vectorization, Undefined Behavior (nsw / poison), instruction selection, register allocation, ThinLTO, and the November 2026 frontier.",
  "nav.back": "← Knowledge index",
