  "ch3.say.ssa": "The renaming walk places <em>{phis} phi node(s)</em> at dominance frontier <em>{df}</em> and mints {vers} single-assignment versions, collapsing {bmem} stack accesses down to <em>{amem}</em>.",
  "ch3.say.alloca": "Without <code>mem2reg</code>, both branches mutate the same stack slot, forcing <em>{bmem} memory loads and stores</em> across the merge.",
  "ch3.p4": "Switch the model to <strong>Loop back-edge</strong>: a `phi` appears at the loop `header` because `body` jumps backward into `header` without dominating it (entry arrives from `B0` on iteration zero). In the default diamond, 1 `phi` node eliminates all 7 stack ops down to 0.",
  "ch3.limit": "The model omits address-taken variables (when `&amp;x` escapes to an unknown pointer): any `alloca` whose pointer might be aliased must stay on the stack unless scalar replacement can prove every access offset.",
  "ch4.title": "The Pass Pipeline: Iterating Tiny Rules to a Fixed Point",
  "toc.ch4": "Fixed-point pass pipeline",
  "ch4.law": "LLVM's optimizer is not one giant brain; it is a queue of focused passes where one pass exposes algebraic constants that let the next pass prune dead control flow, repeating until a full sweep makes zero changes—the fixed point.",
  "ch4.p1": "Consider this tiny function, representative of code produced after C macro or C++ template expansion:",
  "ch4.p2": "<pre class=\"code\">int dead_branch(int x) {   int a = x * 2 + 0;   int b = a - a;   if (b != 0) return 999;   return a + 3; }</pre>",
  "ch4.p3": "No single pass finishes the job alone. <code>SROA</code> removes stack allocations; <code>InstCombine</code> handles local algebra (rewriting <code>x * 2</code> to shift-left <code>shl 1</code>, dropping <code>+ 0</code>, folding <code>a - a</code> to <code>0</code>, and turning <code>icmp ne 0, 0</code> into constant <code>false</code>), yet leaves basic blocks intact; <code>SimplifyCFG</code> sees <code>br i1 false</code> and deletes the unreachable <code>999</code> block while fusing the entry and exit blocks; finally <code>ADCE</code> sweeps away dead values.",
  "dg.pipeline.cap": "Figure 4. Middle-end pass loop in LLVM's New Pass Manager. Each pass matches simple local idioms, exposing cleanups for its neighbors until the IR reaches a fixed point.",
  "dg.pipeline.aria": "Diagram: SROA, InstCombine, SimplifyCFG+GVN, and ADCE chained with a dashed feedback loop to fixed point",
  "dg.pipeline.p1": "Promote allocas",
  "dg.pipeline.p2": "Fold & combine",
  "dg.pipeline.p3": "Prune CFG & GVN",
  "dg.pipeline.p4": "Sweep dead code",
  "dg.pipeline.fix": "Fixed point",
  "ch4.p4": "On host Apple Clang 21.0.0 (`-mllvm -debug-pass=Structure` and `-mllvm -print-after=instcombine`), `dead_branch` shrinks from 11 unoptimized IR ops across 3 major pass stages down to just 3 live ops (`shl nsw`, `add nsw`, and `ret`), erasing `999` completely from the compiled binary.",
  "ch4.model.title": "Fixed-Point Optimization Pass Stepper",
  "ch4.model.how": "Choose an IR snippet and click \"Step Next Pass\" to watch individual rules shrink instructions round by round, or click \"Run to Fixed Point\" to jump to convergence.",
